syntax:
The core syntax involves using iterators with STL containers:

```c++
std::vector<int> vec = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5};
for (auto it = vec.begin(); it != vec.end(); ++it) {
  //Process *it
}

std::list<int> lst = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5};
for (auto it = lst.begin(); it != lst.end(); ++it) {
  //Process *it
}
```
Note the difference in performance characteristics between these loops, despite similar syntax. The compiler generates different assembly instructions based on the iterator type.
